#errorCatcher Echo
#encoding UTF-8
##
## Every month the station has recorded, and every day of the current year.
##
## Not the answers, the numbers behind them. A page works out the wettest year,
## the coldest day or this year against the average from these, without WeeWX
## having to know in advance which of those anyone will ask for.
##
## Months are cheap: fourteen years is 168 rows. Days are not -- fourteen years
## is over five thousand -- so only the current year carries them. That is the
## span where a single day is still worth naming, and it keeps the file small
## enough to fetch on every page load.
##
## This is a Cheetah template that writes JSON rather than HTML. Every tag a
## report can use is available, which is why the aggregates need no generator of
## their own: a template answers anything a tag answers, and computes only what
## is written here.
##
## It is expensive -- one query per figure per row -- so 'stale_age' in skin.conf
## holds it to once a day. A month that has ended never changes again.
##
#set $out = {'generated': $current.dateTime.raw, 'units': {}, 'months': {}, 'days': {}}
##
## Which unit each figure is in. The page converts from these, using the table
## the JSON generator writes into index.json.
